{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EkrrkG9ZPSn8KGGJ2stmsx","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on the context filesystem, here's what I found about the cluster mirroring design RPC methods:\\\\n\\\\n## RPC Method Renaming\\\\n\\\\nIn **KIP-1279: Cluster Mirroring**, the original RPC method names were changed for clarity:\\\\n\\\\n**Original names:**\\\\n- `AddTopicsToMirror`\\\\n- `RemoveTopicsFromMirror`\\\\n\\\\n**Final names:**\\\\n- `StartMirrorTopics`\\\\n- `StopMirrorTopics`\\\\n\\\\n## Reason for Rename\\\\n\\\\nAccording to Federico Valeri's comment (April 15, 2026), the naming was confusing because \\\\\\\"add/remove along with pause/resume is confusing.\\\\\\\" The new names provide better semantic clarity:\\\\n\\\\n- **StartMirrorTopics**: For failback or resuming mirroring\\\\n- **StopMirrorTopics**: For failover or migration use cases\\\\n\\\\nThe same semantics were preserved with the new names, and the terminology was further clarified with separate pause/resume commands for maintenance operations.\\\\n\\\\nAndrew Schofield approved this change, noting that \\\\\\\"start/stop/pause/resume is definitely nicer\\\\\\\" (April 21, 2026).\\\\n\\\\n**Sources:**\\\\n- `/store/kips/KIP-1279/2026-04-15-discuss-cluster-mirroring-d1515ee7.md` (lines 43-46)\\\\n- `/store/kips/KIP-1279/2026-04-30-mail-d143b0b41a8baaf69dfb3a1d-b13eb2ca.md` (lines 73-77)\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1279/2026-03-16-mail-discuss-cluster-mirroring-b980b885.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1279/2026-04-15-discuss-cluster-mirroring-d1515ee7.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1279/2026-04-30-mail-d143b0b41a8baaf69dfb3a1d-b13eb2ca.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":27.69,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":2,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":134447,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":45690,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.11342170000000001,\\\"input_tokens\\\":42,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1711}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"sessi